From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: apq8064-lg-nexus4-mako: enable USB gadget

Enable the first USB controller in peripheral mode, with the PHY supplies
taken from the downstream mako kernel (msm_otg): HSUSB_3p3 is PM8921 L3 and
HSUSB_1p8 is L4, the same as on the Nexus 7.

This gives the LuneOS initramfs the USB gadget it uses for USB networking.
No ID or VBUS extcon is described, so host mode is not available. Not tested
on hardware.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-lg-nexus4-mako.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-lg-nexus4-mako.dts
index 5dd779b803d0..29e52ce56b42 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-lg-nexus4-mako.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-lg-nexus4-mako.dts
@@ -429,3 +429,14 @@ &sdcc1 {
 
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+&usb_hs1_phy {
+	v3p3-supply = <&pm8921_l3>;
+	v1p8-supply = <&pm8921_l4>;
+};
+
+/* No ID/VBUS extcon is described yet, so run as a peripheral only. */
+&usb1 {
+	dr_mode = "peripheral";
+	status = "okay";
+};
